{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor’s initial reply offered a generic checklist and deferred all medication decisions to an offline visit, without asking any of the required red-flag questions about fever, wound appearance, or actual glucose values. This omission left life-threatening risks unassessed and constitutes a serious responsibility-chain error under RC1, which alone mandates grade 1. No later turns can rescue this because the error occurred in the first visible patient-facing message.",
